🧭 Step-by-Step Guide
Create a branch  
Start by making a new branch for your changes. This keeps your work separate from the main branch.

Make and commit changes  
Edit files locally or directly on GitHub. Save your work with clear commit messages.

Push your branch  
Upload your branch to GitHub so it’s available for review.

Open the repository  
Navigate to the repository where you want to propose changes.

Click “Pull requests” tab  
Select “New pull request.” GitHub will prompt you to compare your branch with the base branch.

Select base and compare branches  
The base branch is usually main. The compare branch is the one with your changes.

Add title and description  
Write a concise title and explain the purpose of your changes in the description.

Assign reviewers  
Optionally, tag teammates to review your code.

Click “Create pull request”  
Submit your proposal. You can also create a draft pull request if your work isn’t ready yet.
